WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.480
Firelink Shrine is a rather terrible place, when you think about it.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.720
Sure, the Fire Keeper will always be there for you, but what about when you're not there for her?

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.040
She's disposable, forgotten, just like Champion Gundyr

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.720
who's stranded in another dimension.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.840
Or like the Handmaiden, chained to this fate for what must feel like an eternity.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.280
"Remember well, I am undead.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.080
Bound forever by the Shrine's curse."

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.600
As the fire is linked, over and over

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.480
kingdoms change, and so too does the Shrine.  In this world, as we know, the Shrine is a literal graveyard of ash.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.240
Quite befitting of an exhausted world.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:51.500
Though, one constant through it all is the suffering of the Fire Keepers.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.440
These women aren't as selfless as you might think.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.680
No, they're prisoners, just like you,

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:02.800
and they fight for the linking of the fire, for with the linking of the fire comes rest.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.480
"Finally, the curse of the undead will be lifted,

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.640
and I can die human."

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.520
"Long have I awaited one such as you.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.440
One who can set me free."

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.240
"Ashen One, link the fire.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.160
For the Lords of Cinder,

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:25.470
for the ashen prisoners, for all those held to preserve the fire.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.960
Link the first flame."

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:35.880
Though as we've come to learn, this rest is temporary, and the curse never was lifted.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.360
And yet, the legend of the linking of the fire continues to infect the minds of many.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:47.880
Undead are shepherded towards the first flame, and the kingdoms of the gods are always designed to

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.840
enable their sacrifice in some way.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:56.500
Have you ever noticed that the incinerating kiln is never too far from the kingdom of men?

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.760
Firelink Shrine is a crumbled peak of New Londo.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.840
The Throne of Want sits below Drangleic Castle.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.760
And in Lothric, hidden behind the King's Garden, along a trail of

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.640
ash and untended graves, is the current iteration of Firelink Shrine

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:20.560
and what must be the thousandth firekeeper capable of sending us forward to be face to face

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.160
with Cinder itself.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.040
"Surrender your fires

00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:27.040
to the true heir.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.240
Let him grant death

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.200
to the old gods of Lordran,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.080
Deliverers of the first flame."

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:42.760
Those that fail to become Cinder are cremated, all the same: their ashes scattered in the Untended

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:48.120
Graves by the Soul of Cinder.  Those that succeed become Lords of Cinder,

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.320
but, it says a lot about the future that they fight for if

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.920
our Lords have refused to fight for it a second time.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.360
And so, the grand betrayal was conceived,

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:08.400
this betrayal of the flame was not a novel concept by any means, but perhaps it was still a necessary one, considering

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:14.060
it led to the link of fire being threatened, and the bell tolling for the Unkindled.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:21.560
According to his cinders, the Prince Lothric was destined to be a Lord of Cinder, and was cherished by the royal family,

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:30.480
though ironically, he was born ill, shriveled, and frail, unable even to wield the platinum sword that was his birthright.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:35.340
Conversely, Lothric's older brother, Lorian, was a great champion of the realm.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:42.640
While his younger brother's sword would never be wielded, his was scorched black by the flame of the Demon Prince,

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.240
which he had slain single-handedly.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:53.080
The great tragedy that's referenced so often in their lore is surely that while Prince Lothric was chosen to be a Lord of Cinder,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.880
Prince Lorian was the one suited for it.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:04.440
And so, Lorian must have had a great love for his brother, for he embraced Lothric's curse, merging their two souls.

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:11.959
Tragically, this left Lorian mute and crippled, yet it is said that Lorian indeed wished it so all the same.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.560
There's this great mention of the grief of the Twin Princes, for once they came

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.480
together, they rejected everything that had made this sacrifice necessary.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:28.240
So instead of linking the flame, they settled in their throne room and simply watched the fire fade from a distance

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.780
and with their strength combined, fought off any who would seek their cinders.

00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:40.579
"Ill starred are they who take the throne. I shall not stand among them. The firelinking curse,

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.250
the legacy of lords,

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.580
let it all fade into nothing.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:52.720
Mark my words, Ashen One.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.720
You remain

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.120
among the accursed."

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.100
If we were to join them in their rest,

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.620
this is the fate that the Princes would have us live,

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.380
a darkened Shrine, most likely their Shrine, is hidden behind the chambers of the Consumed King.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.040
And items tell us that if a place is devoid of light,

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:24.889
so too will it be devoid of time. Perhaps this explains away the terrible convolution within this place,

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:31.430
justifying how those in the future shrine can be pulled to this realm, like the Sword Master,

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.640
justifying how we physically walk here from present day Lothric,

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:42.120
and accounting for the dead firekeeper who is from the past, and tucked away.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.120
But of all the things here from past, present, or future,

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:54.160
she is the most consequential, for she is the one that's holding the Eyes that enable a Fire Keeper to

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.560
betray the flame.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:03.080
"Ah.  Found her, did we?  And the black eyes that shimmer within, I see.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.760
'Tis is if it were but yesterday.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.840
We did all we could to spare her from them.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.680
Much has happened since.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:21.080
Mayhap I should apprise thee of what the thin light of these eyes might reveal

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.280
to the eyeless Fire Keeper.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.360
Scenes of betrayal,

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.800
things never intended for her ken,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.120
visions of

00:06:32.139 --> 00:06:34.139
this age's end."

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:40.799
The eyes are said to have belonged to the first Fire Keeper, and of all the would be Lords of Cinder,

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:45.960
it makes the most sense for Prince Lothric to have had access to such an heirloom.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:50.909
He is, after all, the descendant of old royalty, inheritor of the throne,

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:57.840
and it seems that he and Lorian coaxed their Fire Keeper to stifle the flame back in their age

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.720
much like we can with the eyes in our possession.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:05.020
Now ask yourself, how does Ludleth know about any of this?

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:11.000
Ludleth refers to the eyes and the woman they're planted upon in the past tense,

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:16.520
it follows that somehow, he linked the flame after the Princes refused to.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:20.840
"Look not in bewilderment as I say

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.900
I linked the fire long ago,

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.300
becoming a Lord of Cinder.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.440
If substantiation be thy want,

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:33.920
set thine eyes upon my charred corpse.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.000
This sad cadaver."

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:42.850
There's something wrong in this dialogue.  Listen to how guilty and how defensive he sounds.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:47.960
A true Lord of Cinder would have no need to constantly reaffirm his or her legitimacy,

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:52.440
and we get closer to the truth on this by listening to him as he sleeps

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:56.240
as he dreams about the nightmarish rite of linking the fire.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:02.700
"Ahh, it singeth, to the bone, it hurts!

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.100
Please, help me!

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.640
Be done with me!

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.740
No! Gods, no! I cannot bear it!

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:15.800
It burns, burns, help me!

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.900
I am a Lord.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.800
A wee flame, belike,

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.260
but I shoulder the world.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:31.460
Forgive me, I am not to blame.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.540
I'm not!"

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:40.800
From his half-burnt corpse to the guilt that we hear, it seems most likely that Ludleth partially linked the flame.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:47.080
Perhaps it's because of him that there's a light in this world at all, that the bell was able to toll for help.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:53.480
Truly though, this story is one that I can't possibly claim to have all the answers to, for example,

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:56.840
was it possible for weak little Ludleth to link the fire

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:02.080
because the Twin Princes had already defeated the Soul of Cinder?  If Ludleth could link it

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:06.140
why couldn't Champion Gundyr?  Who was the first Fire Keeper?

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.680
Why are there Black Knights here?

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:12.200
And why is this place still so dangerous to our Unkindled?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.320
Perhaps this place was laid with defenders for a reason,

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:22.200
for of all the Shrines, this one seems the most geared towards stopping anyone who would dare rise and somehow link the fire.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:25.900
It's difficult and perhaps pointless to come through here.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:33.880
Champion Gundyr did arrive, only to find the Coiled Sword of the Shrine broken in advance, and the Fire Keeper gone.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:40.240
Grave Wardens patrol the graves, are devoted to hemorrhaging any reanimating corpses, and

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.840
the only Fire Keeper that patrols the grounds is a Scholar:

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:49.800
the Daughter of Crystal is drawn to any embers that would walk through this shrine.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:52.650
And of all the things that don't make sense in this story

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:56.099
it does make a lot of sense that there would be a Scholar here,

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:59.190
for the first of the Scholars as you may recall,

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:05.010
is said to have doubted the linking of the fire and was also a private mentor to the royal prince

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:10.979
At the highest peaks of Lothric Castle are the Grand Archives, home to the Scholars.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:16.710
They're the faction with a close relationship to the previous king, Oceiros, who went mad

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:24.160
studying their store of knowledge, and this close relationship between the crown and the Scholars has clearly carried over to the new

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:29.640
young Prince Lothric.  But who was the first Scholar?  There are many candidates

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.640
but many have theorized that it was Aldia.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:38.200
And while all the evidence behind it being Aldia is circumstantial, the rise of the

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.740
Unkindled is certainly something Aldia  would have fought for:

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:48.480
a destiny beyond the scope of light, beyond the reach of dark, a Painted World inhabited by Ash,

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.940
a future born of this world but free of its curses.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:11:01.680
In no small way, the Princes are responsible for the rise of Ash, an unintended consequence of their grand betrayal.

